{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening","id":1479032,"title":"Political Spectrum [Silver Ladder to Free Council] on Mage Awakening","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-17T14:51:41-07:00","id":1479032,"title":"Political Spectrum [Silver Ladder to Free Council] on Mage Awakening","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am trying to make heads and tails of the changes to the Free Council and Silver Ladder <b>in the second edition</b>. It is my understanding that the main gist would be:<ul><li>Silver Ladder is presented as meritocratic but non-democratic.<br /> Singapore. Meritocrats. \u00a8<i>Although we all have human rights, we are not all equal in capabilities, and we have different roles to play in an Awakened society</i>\u00a8</li> <li>Free Council is presented as democratic but non-technocratic.<br /> Sweden. Egalitarians. \u00a8<i>All mages are created equal and we ought to be one mage, one vote society, inequalities strengthen the Exarchs</i>\u00a8</li> </ul>Those are the main tenet that I see on both orders... Am I right? What I am missing, ignoring, or misrepresenting? Can someone explain in detail how both see Mage and Sleeper society functioning right now and posterior to the Exarchs defeated?<br /> <br /> <b>Even better can someone align them to a real-world political party, movement, or ideology? (Classical Liberals, Utilitarians, etc)</b><br /> <br /> <b>If they were newspapers or magazines, who is closer to <i>The Economist, The Times, </i>or<i> The Financial Times</i>?</b><br /> <br /> Please correct my assumptions and mistakes.<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-17-2022, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T15:59:16-07:00","id":1479036,"title":"","content":"Been awhile since I last checked \u2018the big stuff\u2019 like this, but\u2026<br /> <br /> They have contrasting views on the cosmological role of Sleepers.<br /> <br /> The entire Diamond, plus the Pyramid, follows As Above So Below; that Supernal Symbols give substance and meaning to Fallen Patterns. They hold that Sleepers\u2019 cultural ingenuity is not \u2018true\u2019 ingenuity, but results of being inspired by tuggings of Supernal resonance. Of course, they don\u2019t dismiss the entire thing out of hand, because as far as anyone knows humans (Asleep or not) are the only beings who actively \u2018refine\u2019 the Supernal to the Fallen world that way, but the limit is obvious. <br /> <br /> The Council, along with a number of Nameless Orders (including the Tremere) (and I think the Scelesti?) follow As Below So Above. Human activities are not mere mirrors reflecting the Supernal, but are like lanterns and lighthouses to guide it to the Phenomenal World. As mages they of course admit how mighty the Supernal is, but they hold that without Patterns, its Symbols lose context and coherency. Which is why the Council values human culture and traditions and genius so much \u2014 they\u2019re the frontiers of the Supernal, not its patsies. <br /> <br /> For political spectra\u2026 I\u2019d frankly avoid that line, not because of worries of misrepresenting any ideology (though you should care about that too!), but because I think each of the Orders can potentially find a niche comfort spot in any human politics. <br /> <br /> For example, while the Free Council is often associated with liberal democracy and left progressivism in general, you could find a Libertine vehemently defending some \u2018hidebound conservative\u2019 thing like [insert here], because of its cultural significance.<br /> Because, hey, if something persisted throughout the ages despite wear-and-tear, surely it must have both Supernal and Fallen meaning, right?<br /> <br /> Likewise, the Silver Ladder is usually thought of as the conservatives, but a The\u00e1rch will likely support cases of \u2018overthrowing the old order\u2019 because anyone who has the guts and prowess to do so is clearly worthier than the now-stagnant ruling class.<br /> And hey, it\u2019s not like they\u2019re alien to cases of entitled elites forming out of the so-called enlightened revolutionaries \u2014 more-holier-than-thou, replaced by more-correct-than-thou. It\u2019s just the Symbols of the Supernal reflecting itself in the social Patterns of the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> (If you find anything contradicting with the above from the written official material, that\u2019s likely cuz 1) I\u2019m writing this from memory in the subway without referring to the books, and/or 2) I forgot about them, so feel free to point things out)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  Clarity 04-17-2022, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T16:26:35-07:00","id":1479037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening#post1479032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am trying to make heads and tails of the changes to the Free Council and Silver Ladder <b>in the second edition</b>. It is my understanding that the main gist would be:<ul><li>Silver Ladder is presented as meritocratic but non-democratic. They aim for a Singapore-like state. \u00a8<i>Although we all have human rights, we are not all equal in capabilities, and we have different roles to play in an Awakened society</i>\u00a8</li> <li>Free Council is presented as demagogic but democratic. They aim for an egalitarian government. \u00a8<i>All mages are created equal and we ought to be one mage, one vote society, deference to hierarchy strengthens the Exarchs</i>\u00a8</li> </ul>Those are the main tenet that I see on both orders... Am I right? What I am missing, ignoring, or misrepresenting? Can someone explain in detail how both see Mage and Sleeper society functioning right now and posterior to the Exarchs defeated?<br /> <br /> Please correct my assumptions and mistakes.<br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems pretty correct as far as I\u2019m aware. The Silver Ladder believes all humanity deserves to be able to become a Mage, (and being a Mage is better than not), and that the person who leads should learned and wise, and have the ambition to overthrow the gods. They don\u2019t like the state of the world, and are the only faction I\u2019m aware of that has improving the Fallen World and other humanitarian efforts as a mission goal and ethos. In the perspective of the Silver Ladder, Sleepers are Mages that have been forcibly lobotomized or disabled by the Exarch\u2019s curse. Unless they can overcome it, they need to be guided by those who can see and know the Truth. Those who are wise should guide those who aren\u2019t. (This is the part that usually aggravates everyone else, since it can be easily interpreted as patronizing and self serving. Mind you, the Ladder can and will play second fiddle, they just usually are the only ones who want Consilium leadership positions.) A post Exarchs world probably has the Silver Ladder in the place of the Exarchs, and anyone can climb the Ladder to claim their birthright as a God if they wish. Think of it like all those stories where a evil tyrant is overthrown by a good Monarch, who then reigns wisely and well. Only the evil Ruler in question is God.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the Free Council is believes everyone to be equal if not all in the same way, and are relatively fine with the world, if all the Seers were dead. Sleepers *are* Mages, just ones that are passively using their magic to create technology and learn science or folk beliefs. Honestly, Sleepwalkers probably get as much of a vote as Mages do in most Assemblies. A post Exarch world under the Free Council would probably not be that different, except there would be no formal government outside of votes, and being a Mage would be just a extension of another profession, like being cop or being engineer. Or potentially it could end up with Mage: the Ascension metaphysics, where belief and consensus is reality. <br /> <br /> I find the two Orders fascinating, because both hold rebellious ideologies, but in practice they are almost nothing alike.<br /> <br /> Oh you edited to ask about similar stuff IRL. I\u2019m not particularly great at this, so please take what I say with massive grains of salt, but the Silver Ladder is kinda like hardcore Humanitarian, and Pro-Supernal-Magic for everyone, where the Free Council is more True Democracy than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T19:11:21-07:00","id":1479049,"title":"","content":"Thanks to both.<br /> <br /> So does it make sense to have a Silver Ladder member very involved in scientific innovation? Or a Free Councilor making cases for meritocratic governance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T19:58:00-07:00","id":1479055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479049#post1479049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks to both.<br /> <br /> So does it make sense to have a Silver Ladder member very involved in scientific innovation? Or a Free Councilor making cases for meritocratic governance?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh sure. The Silver Ladder actually rates scientists and experts on academic subjects very highly on the Ladder, if I remember right it\u2019s only a few steps down from being a Mage. The Order as a whole just doesn\u2019t think it will lead to Mass Awakening, meaning it\u2019s not in the plan. But Science absolutely improves the living conditions of people, and the Order will approve of anything that helps improve the Human Condition. <br /> <br /> As for the Free Council, well it\u2019s going to be a harder sell, but I believe representational democracy is still in current culture, and technically representatives are meritocratic. As I recall, there are official positions in the Free Council that technically act like party candidates for elections in the bigger Assemblies. Someone arguing for more power to them probably isn\u2019t uncommon, but might draw a few side eyes and uncomfortable opinions of their character from detractors.<br /> <br /> Another thing to remember is that Orders are like political parties. Not everyone toes the party line, no matter how united they may appear from the outside. This goes triple for the Free Council, since they are the roughly braided together Nameless Orders, and thus prone to fraying and internal strife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T21:01:10-07:00","id":1479058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479049#post1479049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So does it make sense to have a Silver Ladder member very involved in scientific innovation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Practical experts are the second-highest unAwakened rung on the Ladder's sorting hierarchy, below spiritual/philosophical leaders and above administrators and bureaucrats. Figuring out how to learn and manipulate the rules of the world is something the Order wants people to do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or a Free Councilor making cases for meritocratic governance? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Trust the experts&quot; is literally Free Council doctrine. Leadership positions just tend to be situational. The position of Strategos is not a universal one, and it exists where and while there's a need for it. Syndics likewise are just the thing that the moniker denotes, which is &quot;people with enough sway in the Assembly to convince other Voters to vote one way or the other.<br /> <br /> It's important to remember that Consilia and Assemblies aren't modes of government except in the broadest sense of &quot;way the mages in an area have agreed to set the rules relating to stuff that goes beyond your personal affairs.&quot; They're local courts and forums, not different wings of the Bureau of Magical Vocations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-17T23:06:38-07:00","id":1479064,"title":"","content":"The Silver Ladder and the Free Council are very alike. They are the two Orders most concerned with the well-being of Sleepers. They are both host to great numbers of visionaries genuinely and self-sacrificingly committed to a utopian dream to empower and free humanity. As each of the two Orders tries to compensate for their characteristic flaw, they can even drift towards resembling the structure and practices of the other Order.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder values solidarity. Thearchs believe in revolution that can construct an ideal and benevolent order which requires cooperation, commitment, and resistance to not only oppressors but to the systems that reinforce and proliferate the oppressive structure itself. They recognize the need for high-level consideration in order to carefully craft that order, but sometimes fall prey to a bias towards authoritative hierarchy and a preference for philosopher-kings.<br /> <br /> The Free Council values self-determination. Libertines don't believe in trusting any form of wisdom that they cannot test against what they know. Wisdom does not come from one source but can and must be gathered from all levels of the community collectively. They're as passionate as the Thearchs in the need to demolish both oppressive groups and the structures that recapitulate that oppression, but are skeptical of hierarchies that could grow over time into pernicious structures themselves. The need to remain fluid, adaptable, and responsive to all those their community serves also makes them vulnerable to more dissolute focus and disorganized movement.<br /> <br /> The Silver Ladder are communists. The Free Council are anarchists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T04:03:28-07:00","id":1479070,"title":"","content":"Oh, I see now.<br /> <br /> I liked the communist / anarchist simile. Who would be the utilitarians or classical liberals here? The Adamantine Arrow? Guardians are utilitarian surely, but what would the Mysterium be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T04:29:15-07:00","id":1479072,"title":"","content":"This analogy breaks down quickly once you get to the other orders. Don't try to fit round pegs in square holes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T06:09:52-07:00","id":1479073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479070#post1479070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians are utilitarian surely</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you figure?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T06:42:13-07:00","id":1479074,"title":"","content":"The Mysterium is an academic and religious entity more than a political one. The Free Council, the Seers of the Throne and the Silver Ladder are all Orders that are basically defined by their 'grand vision' of how society should function, but the Mysterium isn't really all that concerned about 'society'. The Mysterium is mainly concerned with the acquisition of knowledge, the protection of their 'sacred mysteries' and the pursuit or spiritual enlightenment. It's not a political party, it's a mystery cult.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Adamantine Arrow is more concerned with one's own conduct and the general 'way of the warrior' philosophy than any larger Order-wide vision for the world. 'Existence is War', which means that you must learn to fight, so you can protect yourself and what matters to you. 'Service is Mastery', which means that an ideal Arrow warrior must fight for more than just themselves, but different Arrows all pledge themselves to different purposes. 'The Supernal is the Self', which means that your conduct is echoes out into the world beyond you and is reflected in the Supernal, which also lends further importance to the Order's general quest for personal excellence. 'Enlightenment is Honour', which again means that your worth as a warrior is determined by your conduct, your ability to do your duty and overcome challenges the 'right' way. 'Adaptability is Strength' is just generally good advice to keep in mind.<br /> The Arrow is an army, in a sense, but it might just as well be compared to martial philosophical school-... One which places a particular focus on the means, more than the ends.<br /> <br /> I'd get into the Guardians, because they are somewhat more political than the Arrow or Mysterium, but I need to get to bed. it's also worth remembering that the Silver Ladder serves as the political core of the Diamond and thus their ideas for how 'Awakened society' should function have some degree of influence over the other three orders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 04-18-2022, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T06:43:54-07:00","id":1479075,"title":"","content":"I find it very difficult to map the Orders onto real world beliefs. For example, the Arrow's ideology if applied seriously in the real world is basically fascism (like, if you're obsessed with struggle, honour, and the sacredness of the body, you probably also have a black sun tattoo). However, the Arrow aren't real people, they're fictional wizards in a fictional setting, so they're portrayed as not being fascists (generally).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T07:30:27-07:00","id":1479077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479073#post1479073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you figure?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their ethos is doing what must be done for the greater good. Only consequences seem to be taking into account when doing &quot;evil&quot; acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T07:35:22-07:00","id":1479079,"title":"","content":"The Guardians are a messianic religion of sin-eaters who believe that the human soul cannot attain goodness but can only minimize their destructive impact until the divine and perfected one enters the world to reveal the secret of true wisdom.<br /> <br /> The analogy does not stretch this far.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T09:07:36-07:00","id":1479088,"title":"","content":"Edit: I'm going ot get coffee before actually commenting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-18-2022, 12:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T10:53:25-07:00","id":1479092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479064#post1479064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Silver Ladder are communists. The Free Council are anarchists.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an actual communist, I must correct this. The Silver Ladder are Socialists, Communism is the common utopia both orders share, with one believing you need Philosopher-Kings to achieve it, the other believe you need Complete Freedom.<br /> <br /> Just to clarify definitions: Communism describes a society of equals where no state is necessary and the means of production belong to everyone. Socialism is the idea that the best/only way to achieve this society, or approach it, is through a state that organizes society towards this end and stomps threats to it. Anarchism (or at least this branch of Anarchism) is the idea that the best way to achieve this is to tear down the state itself, so no artificial structure can stop individuals from building this society or be used as a tool by power-hungry people.<br /> <br /> Socialism and Communism are used interchangeably on many texts, and sometimes given disparaging definitions, usually by detractors or people with little first-hand understanding. Those definitions above are what you'll see in the <i>Manifesto of the Communist Party</i> by Karl Marx, and other works on Marxist theory (I'm not a Marxist myself, but I find those definitions more effective in describing those political theories without too much bias).<br /> <br /> Other than that, I think you made as good an analogy as possible for those Orders, and I agree that political analogies don't hold so well with the others.<br /> <br /> Even this analogy is sketchy precisely because the game doesn't actually take into account things like economic system or anything, they're at best dealing with the broadest strokes of a political vision without ever going in details about how a political system should work on its many aspects. The bread and butter of political parties is simply not the concern of even those most political Orders, as their focus as such isn't really in dealing with Fallen politics.<br /> <br /> If you have a Mage character that is actually invested in politics it will be unlikely that their political party/ideology has anything to do with their Order unless a specific context calls for it (like the Orders and Exarchs in a city engaging in politics as proxy for their own conflicts). As long as they can justify their ideas to themselves and don't let them interfere with the Order's activities, anything goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T11:16:06-07:00","id":1479093,"title":"","content":"Correction happily accepted, I did fear I'd be eliding some important distinctions, and meant no negative bias in describing either political philosophy.<br /> <br /> I agree, too, that political philosophy doesn't translate into the beliefs or actions of even the two Orders in question. To the degree that it's a useful comparison, it's a comparison of their respective spirit and outlook, the ways they resemble and contrast with one another in attitude. It's not an actual assertion that Thearchs <i>are</i> socialists or that Libertines <i>are</i> anarchists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 04-18-2022, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T17:07:24-07:00","id":1479102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kleptomania</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479074#post1479074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Mysterium is an academic and religious entity more than a political one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting, while the Mysterium doesn't really map to any political ideologies that refer to themselves as liberal, I think much of their outlook and endeavours correspond with the original meaning of &quot;liberal arts&quot; as the sort of thing you learned in the earliest universities.<br /> <br /> Namely, the acquisition of knowledge and refinement of one's own methods of thinking not so much for the sake of acquiring practical technical skills as coming from a belief system that such pursuits were the proper conduct and method of a liberated person (and enabled greater liberation besides).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479075#post1479075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, the Arrow's ideology if applied seriously in the real world is basically fascism (like, if you're obsessed with struggle, honour, and the sacredness of the body, you probably also have a black sun tattoo). However, the Arrow aren't real people, they're fictional wizards in a fictional setting, so they're portrayed as not being fascists (generally).</div> </div> </div> </div>All fascists believe in things related to the value of struggle, integrity, and the refinement of the body, but not everybody who believes in those things is a fascist.<br /> <br /> Certainly the fascist expressions of them probably gain more clarity when they have a bunch of other stuff like &quot;our society is destined, and was way cooler in the past&quot; and &quot;we are being undermined by some subversive element of all-powerful weaklings&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guardians are a messianic religion of sin-eaters who believe that the human soul cannot attain goodness but can only minimize their destructive impact until the divine and perfected one enters the world to reveal the secret of true wisdom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, when I started reading the original Guardians book a fairly short while ago and seeing its references to how much they like things such as koans and obscure parables to convey their teachings, I became very attached to the idea that large sections of the Order regarding &quot;the Hieromagus will fulfil the Diamond Wheel&quot; literally as a fairly recent development. Kind of an interpretation that gained a lot of traction as a response to a sense of malaise after World War II.<br /> <br /> That for much of the history of the Guardians of the Veil, the attitude that the world will only be fully perfected and redeemed when a perfect Awakened human comes into existence is a coded way of teaching that there will not and cannot ever be a utopia. That the struggle to perfect the world is valuable in its own right, but there will never be an end to it. In times past, susceptibility to a false Hieromagus was regarded as a sign of ignorance, but also an understandable sense of overwhelming desperation.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-18T19:14:04-07:00","id":1479109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479102#post1479102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All fascists believe in things related to the value of struggle, integrity, and the refinement of the body, but not everybody who believes in those things is a fascist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar203_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"203\" data-vbnamecard=\"203\">Kleptomania</a> got it right that the Arrow is more about personal ethos of martial noblesse than about an ideal society.<br /> <br /> This ethos does have a place in politics, as it relates to military castes through history justifying their social position, but it depends a lot on context and the greater system around specific instances of this ethos. Fascism loves the way this ethos romanticize the warrior, and it does have some extra sway among the military because few if any other ideologies directly do so nowadays. But they're not the same thing even IRL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T13:15:28-07:00","id":1479148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479102#post1479102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All fascists believe in things related to the value of struggle, integrity, and the refinement of the body, but not everybody who believes in those things is a fascist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're downplaying how strongly those values are expressed. It's not just knowing the value of struggle, it's Existence is War. It's not 'integrity', they <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">specifically use the word</span></span></span> 'honour'. They don't just believe in getting a bit fitter, it's a metaphysical goal. My point isn't about people believing in these things, it's about making these the foundational pillars of your personal ideology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and &quot;we are being undermined by some subversive element of all-powerful weaklings&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Well, this is where my point about the Arrow being fictional comes in. Like, they do actually have really horrible eternal enemies to fight, they don't have to make one up. Their ideas about honour and the sacredness of the body are at least to some degree true.<br /> <br /> The question was about what kind of real world ideology do the Orders map onto? And my answer was that it's somewhat difficult due to (for example) the Arrow (and by extension the other Orders) being fictional creations in a <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">fictional </span></span></span>situation. To be clear, I was not saying that the Arrow are fascists. I was saying that expressed outside the context of the setting, their ideology would almost certainly be fascism of some variety.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T18:02:37-07:00","id":1479153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479093#post1479093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correction happily accepted, I did fear I'd be eliding some important distinctions, and meant no negative bias in describing either political philosophy.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was well done, just as good a moment as any to clear off common misconception. Actually better precisely because it was good, so it wouldn't result on unnecessary escalation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're downplaying how strongly those values are expressed. It's not just knowing the value of struggle, it's Existence is War. It's not 'integrity', they <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">specifically use the word</span></span></span> 'honour'. They don't just believe in getting a bit fitter, it's a metaphysical goal. My point isn't about people believing in these things, it's about making these the foundational pillars of your personal ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, those things aren't the pillars of Fascism. They're just a facet of it, and they can be a facet of many other things, although currently not so strongly.<br /> <br /> Fascism is about nationalism and hierarchy. It is about controlling society in all its aspects in the name of a romantic (and by nature deluded and murky) national identity, turning the entire population into a permanently mobilized army. While it is obvious that the Warrior Ethos has a strong allure to such an ideology, they're not the same thing. Fascism believes that war and conflict can be good, but usually does not define itself by war, conflict is still secondary, a tool, even if a prized one. Likewise, people that follow the Warrior Ethos believe in it as a moral value and in defending an abstract &quot;us&quot;, but not necessarily that others should be forced into such a structure or that Nation is the better definition for such group.<br /> <br /> You're focusing on how much Fascists tend to be like this, but IRL there are people that strongly favor the Warrior Ethos all over the place in the political spectrum. It is not a balanced distribution, but it is really far from a clear majority towards Fascism or Fascism-like. Most aren't even interested in politics, as this ethos is also heavily about self-identification and discipline, about being instead of about making society be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-19T19:02:39-07:00","id":1479155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're downplaying how strongly those values are expressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think how strongly they're expressed matters. I don't regard fascism as being defined past a threshold of enthusiasm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just knowing the value of struggle, it's Existence is War. It's not 'integrity', they <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">specifically use the word</span></span></span> 'honour'. They don't just believe in getting a bit fitter, it's a metaphysical goal. My point isn't about people believing in these things, it's about making these the foundational pillars of your personal ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arrow book gives a bit more definition to the meaning of that line beyond just &quot;all life is lived for struggle&quot;.<br /> <br /> Numerous real world religions believe in correspondence between spiritual and physical health. The Nazis were in fact cribbing some of their ideas from a few of them. Hinduism springs to mind.<br /> <br /> Honour and integrity are completely interchangeable words.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, they do actually have really horrible eternal enemies to fight, they don't have to make one up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Going by a chapter fiction in the splatbook and one of the core character concepts, one of those enemies is &quot;poverty&quot;.<br /> <br /> They don't need literal monsters to still have an ethos that can be expressed reasonably.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be clear, I was not saying that the Arrow are fascists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well absolutely there were and are Arrows who look at what fascism is about and think &quot;this fits us&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was saying that expressed outside the context of the setting, their ideology would almost certainly be fascism of some variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>This kind of comes back to my point of &quot;fascism believes in all those things, but but all who believe in them are fascists&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can focus on the emphasis or point to the spirituality or require unnecessarily exact terminology, and you're still going to have a Venn diagram that includes but is not limited to fascism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-22T06:39:55-07:00","id":1479293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're downplaying how strongly those values are expressed. It's not just knowing the value of struggle, it's Existence is War. It's not 'integrity', they <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">specifically use the word</span></span></span> 'honour'. They don't just believe in getting a bit fitter, it's a metaphysical goal. My point isn't about people believing in these things, it's about making these the foundational pillars of your personal ideology.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, this is where my point about the Arrow being fictional comes in. Like, they do actually have really horrible eternal enemies to fight, they don't have to make one up. Their ideas about honour and the sacredness of the body are at least to some degree true.<br /> <br /> The question was about what kind of real world ideology do the Orders map onto? And my answer was that it's somewhat difficult due to (for example) the Arrow (and by extension the other Orders) being fictional creations in a <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">fictional </span></span></span>situation. To be clear, I was not saying that the Arrow are fascists. I was saying that expressed outside the context of the setting, their ideology would almost certainly be fascism of some variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Adamantine Arrow isn't authoritarian or nationalistic enough to be fascist. Furthermore, it's profoundly individualistic in a way that runs counter to fascism, though perhaps a better way to put it would be-... Personal. The entire philosophy of the Arrow is about how <b>you</b> act, what <b>you</b> do and <b>your</b> own pursuit of excellence, rather than anything about nation or race.<br /> Now, make no mistake, an individual Adamantine Arrow can be a fascist, but the Order itself isn't even close.<br /> <br /> Do you know what I think would be a better example of a real-life parallel to the ideology of the Adamantine Arrow? Athletes.<br /> The athlete's world is one defined by competition and struggle (Existence is War), wherein they are expected to challenge themselves (Challenge is Magical) and strive towards physical excellence for its own sake (The Supernal is the Self). An athlete is expected to be honourable, they must respect the fairness and general 'sanctity' of the sport, not cheating or using performance enhancing drugs (Enlightenment is Honour). Athletes oftentimes come to represent things greater than themselves, including nations or particular causes (Service is Mastery). As always, Adaptibility is Strength is just generally good advice.<br /> Athletes might not be 'warriors', strictly speaking, but athletic culture fits with a lot of Arrow concepts and can serve as a useful starting point for considering their philosophy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":203,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","user":"Kleptomania","date":". 04-22-2022, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T00:07:24-07:00","id":1479328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're downplaying how strongly those values are expressed. It's not just knowing the value of struggle, it's Existence is War. It's not 'integrity', they <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">specifically use the word</span></span></span> 'honour'. They don't just believe in getting a bit fitter, it's a metaphysical goal. My point isn't about people believing in these things, it's about making these the foundational pillars of your personal ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sacredness of the body thing isn't actually in the 2e corebook, incidentally. It might be in the 1e splatbook or the 1e core, but I don't have access to those right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, this is where my point about the Arrow being fictional comes in. Like, they do actually have really horrible eternal enemies to fight, they don't have to make one up. Their ideas about honour and the sacredness of the body are at least to some degree true.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be clear, the &quot;honour&quot; thing is &quot;in accordance with their ideals, in true harmony with their perfect selves&quot;. It's just a fancy way of saying &quot;be true to yourself&quot;.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1479032-political-spectrum-silver-ladder-to-free-council-on-mage-awakening?p=1479148#post1479148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question was about what kind of real world ideology do the Orders map onto? And my answer was that it's somewhat difficult due to (for example) the Arrow (and by extension the other Orders) being fictional creations in a <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">fictional </span></span></span>situation. To be clear, I was not saying that the Arrow are fascists. I was saying that expressed outside the context of the setting, their ideology would almost certainly be fascism of some variety.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fiction and reality may be separate, but they reflect each other in distorted ways. Being fictional shouldn't give them a pass on being fascist, if they are. If real-world fascists were correct about, as Isator phrases it, &quot;all-powerful weaklings&quot;, they wouldn't stop being fascists. You may as well call the Council fascist. Aren't the Followers of the Lie all-powerful weaklings? The Council isn't as mealy-mouthed about it as the Arrow are. &quot;Existence is War&quot;? Pfah. &quot;Destroy the Followers of the Lie&quot;, more like. Every Order is capable of having members in perfect accord with Order ideals also be fascists. &quot;Sins for a just end grant Wisdom&quot;, after all.<br /> <br /> Giving a bad answer is worse than no answer.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Hence, @Ibeaumanior, the Ladder and the Council can be reasonably mapped onto political ideologies because they're defined in large part in a political manner. The Ladder defines itself through its completion of the Ladder, a political goal, and the Council is marked by the Great Refusal, a political moment that shaped its entire unifying philosophy. The other Orders do not have such direct consequences in politics from their spiritual beliefs.<br /> <br /> A political party or movement is defined by its ideas on things like governance and justice. The Arrow, the Mysterium, and the Guardians do not have unified ideals on such topics; individuals, Legacies, even factions, certainly might, but the Orders themselves provide no real guidance. The Ladder and the Council <i>do</i> have such opinions.<br /> <br /> It may be more fruitful for you to look at how Chinese or Japanese cultures handled the balance of multiple religions in daily life and public ceremony than to look at political spectra: there's a separation of concerns, usually, that lets the average person navigate the different systems of belief, and that's often how Order politics play out in a Consilium. Looking at how political flashpoints in history divided things may help illuminate how coalition-building and side-taking can happen in a Consilium.<br /> <br /> (Also, utilitarianism is an <i>ethical</i> philosophy, not a political one.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}